On Sep 15, 2010, at 4:19 PM, o.mannion at auckland.ac.nz wrote:

> The part I'm not sure about is how to convert the matrix/dataframe to a java reference so I can pass it as a parameter to a java method with .jcall.
> 
> For this can I use toJava?
> 

Well, you can (if you realize what that means), but that only makes sense if you use JRI and you really want just a reference and not the actual data (e.g. if you want to call an R function with the data as an argument without pushing it across...).

So, again - what are you exactly are you trying to do? Do you really use JRI or you have regular Java code underneath? What do you want to have on the Java side - i.e. what do you plan to do there? For most mortals it's as simple as let's say:

m = matrix(rnorm(100), 20)

.jcall(myObject, "V", "setMatrix", as.doubles(m), dim(m))

with the corresponding Java method

public void setMatrix(double matrix[], int dims[]);

if what you really want is the actual data ...

Cheers,
Simon



