Yes, if you are running JRI then you can do that. You'll need to create the proper JRIEngine, so assuming you are in JRI you can use something like:

eng = .jnew("org/rosuda/REngine/JRI/JRIEngine", .jengine())

.jcall(myObject, "V", "display", toJava(mtcars, eng))

if your method is
public void display(REXPReference x);
otherwise (in your example) you'll have to use .jcast accordingly.

Cheers,
Simon



