Just for completeness - the explicit JRIEngine constructor assumes that you don't have any JRIEngine at that point and should be run only once. To make sure that is the case a safe code would do something like this:

e = .jcall("org/rosuda/REngine/REngine", "Lorg/rosuda/REngine/REngine;", "getLastEngine")
if (is.jnull(e)) e = .jnew("org/rosuda/REngine/JRI/JRIEngine", .jengine())

However, it's actually even easier than that, the default (engine=NULL) will perform exactly the checks above so you can safely use toJava(foo) and the only thing you have to ensure is that you run .jengine() sometime in the beginning.

Cheers,
Simon




